1
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:21,350
you stop?

2
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:29,860
Oh, no, no, no,

3
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:22,020
Dreaming on!

4
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:29,080
Whoa!

5
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:50,920
Sir Kin'emon!

6
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:52,260
Sir Denjiro!

7
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:54,020
Godspeed ahead!

8
00:01:54,580 --> 00:01:55,900
And to you as well!

9
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:24,917
We're out of money!

10
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,760
What now? Oops.

11
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:28,060
Oh, no.

12
00:02:28,460 --> 00:02:29,540
What about dinner?

13
00:02:30,140 --> 00:02:30,970
Yes.

14
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:32,180
Here's the plan.

15
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:34,108
Let's head to town and beg.

16
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:35,860
Please, no. Whoa.

17
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:44,480
It must have been hard.

18
00:02:45,060 --> 00:02:46,160
I'm sorry.

19
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:48,970
King.

20
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:52,660
Don't stop.

21
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:54,500
We must go on.

22
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:55,960
Izo?

23
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:04,180
This may be our end.

24
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:05,840
Are you certain?

25
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:09,559
I've missed too many chances
for a meaningful death.

26
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:13,400
Alright, onward.

27
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:18,410
Okiku!

28
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,417
Die alongside your lord if you like,

29
00:03:57,500 --> 00:04:00,477
but wouldn't you rather
conquer the world with me?

30
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:03,517
I know that you, samurai,
are famously loyal,

31
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:10,377
and if any of you have the courage
to challenge us, you have my respect.

32
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:15,577
I speak for all our ninjas

33
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:17,397
as head of the Oniwabanshu;

34
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:19,257
I pledge my forces to you.

35
00:04:19,340 --> 00:04:21,660
We are 5,000 strong.

36
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:28,640
The samurai, who also number 5,000 in
total, pledge their allegiance as well.

37
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:32,740
I welcome you.

38
00:04:38,520 --> 00:04:40,100
Our lord is dead.

39
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:42,480
Well, whatever.

40
00:04:44,320 --> 00:04:45,580
That's great, man.

41
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:47,377
I'm so glad we're not enemies.

42
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:49,257
I didn't want to have to kill you.

43
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:51,100
Here's to a bright future!

44
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:59,060
How dare you call yourself
samurai after that! Not now, boss!

45
00:04:59,220 --> 00:05:00,400
We gotta lay low!

46
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:05,700
Well, what do you know?

47
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:09,334
That idiot's flunkies couldn't
wait to get a new master.

48
00:05:10,980 --> 00:05:12,840
Nice thinking, Kaido.

49
00:05:19,340 --> 00:05:20,800
Ha ha ha ha ha.

50
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:25,940
Our forces are already
coming together nicely.

51
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:30,760
Let me go! Hey! Ow!

52
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:32,100
Don't be a jerk!

53
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:35,200
Keep those slippery Straw Hats restrained!

54
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:41,929
If you think you've
won, you're dead wrong!

55
00:05:42,020 --> 00:05:45,620
As long as Shinobu escapes,
we still have a chance!

56
00:05:46,020 --> 00:05:47,360
Forgive me, Onami.

57
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:48,540
I'm going ahead.

58
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:52,520
I'll be fine, just save Mama!

59
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:58,480
Lord Odin knew from the start, taking
down Orochi doesn't change anything!

60
00:05:59,020 --> 00:06:04,300
For 20 years, Kaido has been our true
enemy, the only target that matters!

61
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:15,760
There's no Shogun in Wano now.

62
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:21,340
All his samurai, all his ninja,
all his men will serve me.

63
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:26,000
The people in the flower
capital don't know a damn thing.

64
00:06:26,340 --> 00:06:31,400
They're dancing the night away in
what'll be their final hours of freedom.

65
00:06:38,820 --> 00:06:42,820
Because I'll say one thing, I've
always had my doubts about you.

66
00:06:43,980 --> 00:06:48,333
It's hard for me to believe that you're
the son of a man like Kozuki Oden.

67
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:51,094
You're nothing but a whimpering coward.

68
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:54,440
That's not true!

69
00:06:57,840 --> 00:07:03,860
This execution serves to bring an end
to the land of Wano as you know it.

70
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:09,820
I've been thinking back to the day 20 years
ago, when we met in the burning castle.

71
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:15,140
I asked a question you never answered.

72
00:07:19,660 --> 00:07:23,120
Oh, someone, help.

73
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:28,640
Now tell me your name, dammit.

74
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:30,580
Spideless brat!

75
00:07:34,780 --> 00:07:35,620
Father!

76
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:38,720
Somebody help!

77
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:50,657
If you're not the son
of Kozuki Odin and Toki,

78
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:53,397
then I'll cancel your
execution immediately!

79
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:57,757
And let you walk free—you
would have my apologies;

80
00:07:57,840 --> 00:08:01,397
it would have been a
great mistake on my part.

81
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:02,310
But

82
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:06,297
if it wasn't an heir?

83
00:08:06,380 --> 00:08:08,577
And you are their son?

84
00:08:08,660 --> 00:08:11,777
You'll suffer the same fate as Odin!

85
00:08:11,860 --> 00:08:13,657
And die by my hand.

86
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:14,570
Now

87
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:22,917
brat—one last time!

88
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,240
last time

89
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:27,240
What is your name?

90
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:30,737
See how generous the commander could be?

91
00:08:30,820 --> 00:08:31,840
Don't worry, kid.

92
00:08:31,980 --> 00:08:33,457
Your dad won't be ashamed of you.

93
00:08:33,540 --> 00:08:35,260
He's been dead for years.

94
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:39,080
Come up with a funny name for us, okay?

95
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:40,600
You got this.

96
00:08:45,140 --> 00:08:48,737
No one will look down on you if
you have to lie, Lord Momonosuke.

97
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:50,440
Just please stay alive.

98
00:08:58,040 --> 00:08:58,870
What?

99
00:08:58,953 --> 00:08:59,783
Are you serious?

100
00:09:00,820 --> 00:09:03,440
That boy is the real Kozuki Momonosuke?

101
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:04,740
Of course he is!

102
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:07,181
Hoden's retainers are alive, too!

103
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:10,230
What?!

104
00:09:13,540 --> 00:09:14,680
The enemy!

105
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:21,580
Get out of my way!

106
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:28,880
You mean the samurai made it?

107
00:09:29,580 --> 00:09:31,660
All of them are alive? Really?

108
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:37,840
So Odin's sacrifice was
worth it. That's great!

109
00:09:38,340 --> 00:09:39,380
He did it!

110
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:42,300
Why are we standing around?

111
00:09:43,100 --> 00:09:45,600
Let's get out there and rescue Momonosuke!

112
00:09:46,900 --> 00:09:48,060
I can't wait!

113
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:51,817
If the Akasai and I are here, then
that means I get to meet them!

114
00:09:51,900 --> 00:09:53,076
Put me down, Yamato!

115
00:09:53,640 --> 00:09:54,470
Huh?

116
00:09:54,553 --> 00:09:55,420
Wait a sec.

117
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:56,797
What did you just call me?

118
00:09:56,880 --> 00:09:59,540
Master Yamato, please stop!

119
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:06,417
Master Yamato and Suha and Luffy are
heading to the floor, moving fast!

120
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:07,937
You mean the performance floor?

121
00:10:08,020 --> 00:10:08,850
Yes, sir!

122
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:11,077
We're closing in to catch them right now!

123
00:10:11,160 --> 00:10:12,180
No, don't bother.

124
00:10:12,460 --> 00:10:13,695
You know Matt's best.

125
00:10:15,540 --> 00:10:17,540
Beating up my men now, are you?

126
00:10:19,900 --> 00:10:20,730
Yamato!

127
00:10:20,813 --> 00:10:22,720
I'm gonna bust you up!

128
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:31,200
Puss up! Stop!

129
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:32,780
We can't go this way!

130
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:35,040
It's too scary! Too scary!

131
00:10:35,280 --> 00:10:36,917
This whole mission is scary!

132
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,118
But you heard them!

133
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:39,692
They're gonna kill Momo!

134
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:41,900
Oh, I know, but look!

135
00:10:42,060 --> 00:10:42,980
Those giants!

136
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:44,680
They'll gobble us up!

137
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:47,468
They'll grind our bones
to make their bread!

138
00:10:48,160 --> 00:10:49,640
We can do this, pal!

139
00:10:50,020 --> 00:10:52,697
Even an emperor of the sea
couldn't take us out, right?

140
00:10:52,780 --> 00:10:56,900
If Big Mom can't beat General
Franky, then no one can!

141
00:10:57,800 --> 00:10:59,080
I don't care!

142
00:10:59,400 --> 00:11:00,900
They're still too scary!

143
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:02,621
Don't freak out!

144
00:11:02,900 --> 00:11:04,580
You're scaring me too!

145
00:11:05,180 --> 00:11:06,600
Take Commander Jumper!

146
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:07,819
What's your order?

147
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:12,080
Retreat! Retreat!

148
00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:21,620
What is your deal?

149
00:11:23,580 --> 00:11:26,260
You're a samurai, huh? So what?

150
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:28,988
Because I'm going to
be king of the pirates!

151
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:33,100
Your father's a great man.

152
00:11:34,260 --> 00:11:36,980
Momonosuke, one day you
will rule this land.

153
00:11:37,180 --> 00:11:38,533
Then you'll understand.

154
00:11:48,780 --> 00:11:52,040
You want to know the
meaning of your name? Yes!

155
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:56,140
I want you to be strong,

156
00:11:56,400 --> 00:12:00,106
but more than that you should be
compassionate and broad-minded

157
00:12:04,900 --> 00:12:05,730
Momo

158
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:11,480
It's a word that means perilous among men

159
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:15,300
You want my name?

160
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:17,800
It's Kozuki Momonosuke.

161
00:12:18,620 --> 00:12:20,037
Hear me now!

162
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:25,540
Now I shall become the
Shogun of the land of Wano!

163
00:12:33,780 --> 00:12:35,680
Of course you will, my lord!

164
00:12:37,260 --> 00:12:39,080
I'm coming, Lord Momonosuke.

165
00:12:39,420 --> 00:12:41,200
I promise I'll save you.

166
00:12:42,640 --> 00:12:45,440
It seems the future of
Wano is in good hands.

167
00:12:45,780 --> 00:12:47,309
We're almost there, Luffy!

168
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:51,306
Let me take these things off.

169
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:53,260
I promise, right? Yes, please.

170
00:12:55,620 --> 00:12:59,420
But, uh, just in case, could
you throw them far away?

171
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:02,920
I don't think they'll
explode, but I can't be sure.

172
00:13:12,980 --> 00:13:14,557
What's wrong with this country?

173
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:16,920
You're nothing but fools!

174
00:13:25,440 --> 00:13:26,640
Father... Mother...

175
00:13:27,680 --> 00:13:31,420
I am a disappointment
to you and to myself.

176
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:34,157
All I wanted was to be able to face you

177
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:36,887
with pride when we
reunited in the afterlife.

178
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:40,477
Iori, I wish I could see you again.

179
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:44,060
If even for a moment, I don't want to die!

180
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:45,900
Curse these tears!

181
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:49,666
Osamu and I should not
cry in front of others!

182
00:13:50,020 --> 00:13:51,720
I am ashamed!

183
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:03,600
You took them off!

184
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:12,800
Luffy, it was true!

185
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:17,180
Go to hell, you stupid
ugly cow, gorilla bastard!

186
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:21,480
You really were going to kill me!

187
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:25,600
Where the hell did that
explosion come from?

188
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:27,760
Somebody figure it out right now!

189
00:14:35,180 --> 00:14:36,820
Well, that settles it.

190
00:14:37,340 --> 00:14:38,897
I've made up my mind.

191
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:41,060
You're not my father anymore!

192
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:46,680
Whatever trouble you're starting,
you better knock it off!

193
00:14:55,820 --> 00:14:57,680
Come back, Yamato!

194
00:14:58,120 --> 00:15:00,180
I'll crush you!

195
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:11,340
I'm glad we weren't too late, but
this isn't our fight to start.

196
00:15:17,780 --> 00:15:21,980
That honor belongs to somebody
else, and you know who it is.

197
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:34,340
Yaku!

198
00:16:00,180 --> 00:16:01,010
Hey!

199
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:32,330
Huh?

200
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,760
The Akazaya Samurai!

201
00:16:35,020 --> 00:16:36,720
Where did they come from?

202
00:16:41,720 --> 00:16:42,550
What?

203
00:16:42,633 --> 00:16:43,817
The kings of the minx?

204
00:16:43,900 --> 00:16:45,076
They're still alive?

205
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:50,660
They won't lose to a bunch of ghosts!

206
00:16:56,340 --> 00:16:57,170
Izo!

207
00:17:00,180 --> 00:17:02,020
Hey, you shit-heads!

208
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:04,980
Stop drinking and come kick some ass!

209
00:17:05,340 --> 00:17:07,020
The party is up!

210
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:08,700
We're under attack!

211
00:17:10,740 --> 00:17:13,400
It's you, Kyoshiro!

212
00:17:15,440 --> 00:17:16,270
Kaido!

213
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:22,280
I'll kill you as many times as it takes!

214
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:29,960
Surrender your name.

215
00:17:30,820 --> 00:17:32,440
Thee as a child.

216
00:17:33,580 --> 00:17:36,017
The blades you wield are powerless.

217
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:38,040
They can't cut me.

218
00:17:46,160 --> 00:17:48,720
Stake your very lives on this attack.

219
00:17:51,580 --> 00:17:52,897
Odin.

220
00:17:52,980 --> 00:17:55,497
Leave the land of water.

221
00:17:55,580 --> 00:17:57,980
And never return.

222
00:18:12,420 --> 00:18:13,820
Tsunami.

223
00:18:34,720 --> 00:18:36,920
Holden Two-Swords die!

224
00:18:38,300 --> 00:18:40,160
Paradise Ports die!

225
00:18:48,720 --> 00:18:51,240
I feel it in the old scar Odin gave me.

226
00:18:51,740 --> 00:18:53,880
How did the blades pierce my flesh?

227
00:18:54,140 --> 00:18:55,540
Why does it burn?

228
00:18:57,380 --> 00:19:01,000
You have underestimated my samurai, Kaido.

229
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:03,840
They can call me a hero or a fool.

230
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:08,160
They can even forget me if they so please.

231
00:19:08,840 --> 00:19:09,670
But...

232
00:19:14,020 --> 00:19:18,040
No matter what, my spirit will live on!

233
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:28,520
This shouldn't be possible.

234
00:19:29,060 --> 00:19:31,320
Are they using Ryu like Odin did?

235
00:19:35,580 --> 00:19:37,360
Pierce him through!

236
00:20:05,700 --> 00:20:09,440
It's really them, the Akazai
Samorais. Yeah, I know.

237
00:20:09,700 --> 00:20:10,560
Cool, huh?

238
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:14,300
This is my second bloody party in a row.

239
00:20:14,780 --> 00:20:16,957
You're not dead down
there, are you, Kaido?

240
00:20:17,040 --> 00:20:18,880
Now get in there!

241
00:20:19,100 --> 00:20:21,500
Slaughter those Akazara rats!

242
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:26,800
So Straw Hat and the
others were just decoys.

243
00:20:27,140 --> 00:20:29,637
They were coven for the
samurai surprise attack.

244
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:31,308
Keep your eyes peeled, men.

245
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:34,940
If those samurai snuck in,
there might be more intruders.

246
00:20:35,220 --> 00:20:36,800
You bet there are!

247
00:20:47,040 --> 00:20:47,870
Yeah.

248
00:21:10,600 --> 00:21:12,720
Listen, you spineless thugs.

249
00:21:12,980 --> 00:21:15,686
I won't let you lay a
finger on those samurai.

250
00:21:16,040 --> 00:21:18,520
Come on, let's get in there and fight!

251
00:21:18,760 --> 00:21:20,701
I could go for some payback, too!

252
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:23,080
I found you, Yamato!

253
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:25,480
Now get rid!

254
00:21:28,180 --> 00:21:29,010
Headbutt!

255
00:21:32,100 --> 00:21:33,280
O .T.

256
00:21:39,640 --> 00:21:42,097
How dare you clobber me with that club!

257
00:21:42,180 --> 00:21:45,437
I am supposed to be
your ally and now you're

258
00:21:45,520 --> 00:21:48,320
running around and playing
hero with Straw Hat.

259
00:21:48,440 --> 00:21:50,460
That's ever ever so messed up

260
00:21:51,300 --> 00:21:53,317
There's nothing messed up about it,

261
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:58,460
but this is the day that I
will become Kozuki Oden Huh?

262
00:21:58,940 --> 00:22:00,780
You totally lost me.

263
00:22:00,940 --> 00:22:02,352
Ah, you're such an idiot

264
00:22:03,960 --> 00:22:07,557
Master Yamato we need
your help the commander

265
00:22:07,640 --> 00:22:10,237
just got attacked by the
Akazaya samurai All right,

266
00:22:10,320 --> 00:22:12,457
we've got invaders running
all over the place.

267
00:22:12,540 --> 00:22:14,897
Whatever you're doing now is not the time.

268
00:22:14,980 --> 00:22:15,810
I disagree.

269
00:22:15,940 --> 00:22:17,277
I'm not your ally anymore.

270
00:22:17,360 --> 00:22:18,840
I am your enemy, in fact.

271
00:22:19,060 --> 00:22:21,800
And I don't care if my father dies. What?

272
00:22:22,560 --> 00:22:24,540
More chaos, I see.

273
00:22:24,840 --> 00:22:27,480
Never a dull moment at this party, huh?

274
00:22:28,120 --> 00:22:29,120
Come, go!

275
00:22:31,580 --> 00:22:32,920
Alpha, I die!

276
00:22:36,300 --> 00:22:37,620
Wait a minute.

277
00:22:51,280 --> 00:22:52,540
That's not good.

278
00:22:52,800 --> 00:22:54,200
Did she notice Luffy?

279
00:23:04,860 --> 00:23:07,240
I can't deal with Big Mom!

280
00:23:07,460 --> 00:23:08,800
I got a job to do!

281
00:23:09,920 --> 00:23:12,600
It's Draw Hat Luffy!

282
00:23:12,940 --> 00:23:15,840
I have you now!

283
00:23:29,920 --> 00:23:31,320
Faulty...

284
00:23:32,880 --> 00:23:34,060
Mortar!

285
00:23:45,960 --> 00:23:47,480
You ready, Carrot?

286
00:23:47,620 --> 00:23:48,680
It's time to go!

287
00:23:49,620 --> 00:23:50,450
Right!

288
00:23:53,280 --> 00:23:54,800
You're in for it now!

289
00:23:56,760 --> 00:23:58,000
Black balls!

290
00:24:01,900 --> 00:24:04,220
Whoa, buddy! What did you do?

291
00:24:05,220 --> 00:24:06,800
This is gonna hurt!

292
00:24:07,440 --> 00:24:09,157
And I got something too!

293
00:24:09,240 --> 00:24:11,800
One squirm cloud coming your way!

294
00:24:17,180 --> 00:24:18,560
Alley cloud?

295
00:24:24,480 --> 00:24:25,520
Epo!

296
00:24:25,820 --> 00:24:27,340
Ectoclasm Center!

297
00:24:45,540 --> 00:24:46,370
Nailed it!

298
00:24:50,740 --> 00:24:54,000
You think you can kick dirt
in the face of my family?

299
00:24:54,280 --> 00:24:56,515
You think I was going to let you live?

300
00:24:58,620 --> 00:25:00,660
I came here for you.

301
00:25:01,040 --> 00:25:04,420
That is to say, I came here to kill you!

302
00:25:05,740 --> 00:25:06,860
Straw Hat!

303
00:25:09,260 --> 00:25:11,680
What brings you to the land of Wano?

304
00:25:12,200 --> 00:25:15,620
You don't actually think you
can take down Kaido, do you?

305
00:25:15,940 --> 00:25:18,140
What a laugh, you little kidder.

306
00:25:18,240 --> 00:25:20,100
That's not why I'm here!

307
00:25:22,920 --> 00:25:23,750
Luffy!

308
00:25:28,660 --> 00:25:29,490
Mr.

309
00:25:29,573 --> 00:25:31,362
Straw Hat Man, what did you say?

310
00:25:31,540 --> 00:25:33,320
If that's not it, then why?

311
00:25:34,500 --> 00:25:37,380
I won't stop at Kaido.

312
00:25:40,740 --> 00:25:43,677
Orochi said that after 20 years,

313
00:25:43,760 --> 00:25:47,080
the Akazaya Samurai would
come to get their revenge.

314
00:25:47,920 --> 00:25:50,457
Everyone thought he was
just being paranoid.

315
00:25:50,540 --> 00:25:53,300
Then one by one, the pieces came together.

316
00:25:56,520 --> 00:26:00,157
But even Orochi didn't think
you would team up with pirates.

317
00:26:00,240 --> 00:26:04,680
It seems they were among the so-called
ghosts appearing at Odin Castle.

318
00:26:05,160 --> 00:26:06,720
Reports from Punk Hazard.

319
00:26:07,040 --> 00:26:08,660
The battle in Dressrosa.

320
00:26:08,880 --> 00:26:10,520
Your allies in Zou.

321
00:26:11,640 --> 00:26:15,180
All threads that were tied
together by the Straw Hats.

322
00:26:16,920 --> 00:26:18,620
Funny how it all worked out.

323
00:26:18,780 --> 00:26:20,917
I've been eyeing Straw Hat for some time,

324
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:23,647
and yet there you were,
hiding in his shadow.

325
00:26:24,660 --> 00:26:26,860
Some of you held out for 20 years.

326
00:26:27,320 --> 00:26:28,897
Some leapt forward in time.

327
00:26:28,980 --> 00:26:34,297
and you gathered an
impressive army but watch

328
00:26:34,380 --> 00:26:37,597
out cuz pirates will stab you in the back.

329
00:26:37,680 --> 00:26:44,097
The second Straw Hat realizes you're
gonna lose; he'll turn tail and leave you.

330
00:26:44,180 --> 00:26:49,357
Besides, I've already taken him down
a peg once he's useless as an ally.

331
00:26:49,440 --> 00:26:53,300
I have heard more than enough
of your baseless slander.

332
00:26:54,840 --> 00:26:57,100
Sir Luffy is nothing like you.

333
00:26:58,120 --> 00:27:01,837
You Kaido, Onuchi, and all
of your stupid friends too.

334
00:27:01,920 --> 00:27:03,777
You're getting your asses kicked.

335
00:27:03,860 --> 00:27:05,837
Every last one of you.

336
00:27:05,920 --> 00:27:07,677
You mark my words.

337
00:27:07,760 --> 00:27:10,257
He will stand at the
pinnacle of this sea someday.

338
00:27:10,340 --> 00:27:12,997
Even if every last one of us dies.

339
00:27:13,080 --> 00:27:14,497
Sir Luffy will remain.

340
00:27:14,580 --> 00:27:17,317
Jaybreak will come to
the land of Wano again.

341
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:18,860
It shall be.

342
00:27:19,680 --> 00:27:22,200
Because that's what we promised our lord.

343
00:27:24,520 --> 00:27:27,180
It's going to be an Alto war!

344
00:27:31,640 --> 00:27:33,220
Awfully cocky, aren't you?

345
00:27:33,460 --> 00:27:36,754
What are you going to do with
just a few hundred troops?

346
00:27:43,680 --> 00:27:45,920
What she said, idiot!

347
00:27:49,420 --> 00:27:50,460
Ta-da-da-da-da!

348
00:27:51,620 --> 00:27:52,720
Yes, sir.

349
00:27:52,840 --> 00:27:54,060
It's an emergency!

350
00:27:54,620 --> 00:27:58,502
Thousands of intruders are pouring
in from the back of the castle!

351
00:27:59,440 --> 00:28:00,270
Whoa!

352
00:28:01,780 --> 00:28:03,220
That's impossible!

353
00:28:08,340 --> 00:28:09,280
Let's go!

354
00:28:16,660 --> 00:28:17,977
All right, fine.

355
00:28:18,060 --> 00:28:19,940
If that's what you want.

356
00:28:27,580 --> 00:28:31,120
Come on, I can do this
all day. Is that a joke?

357
00:28:31,340 --> 00:28:33,620
The only joke here is you!

358
00:28:39,140 --> 00:28:39,970
Samurai.

359
00:28:46,220 --> 00:28:47,060
Cezara Judo!

360
00:28:47,540 --> 00:28:48,952
We are here to help you!

361
00:28:49,220 --> 00:28:50,320
This is point C!

362
00:28:50,560 --> 00:28:53,497
The samurai who got caught in
the flower capital are here!

363
00:28:53,580 --> 00:28:57,992
They're teaming up with the prisoners
from Udon and kicking our butts hard!

364
00:29:25,640 --> 00:29:26,717
Let's keep it up.

365
00:29:26,800 --> 00:29:28,860
We don't want to fall behind.

366
00:29:31,740 --> 00:29:33,497
What a gentleman you are.

367
00:29:33,580 --> 00:29:34,877
Clearing the way for us.

368
00:29:34,960 --> 00:29:35,917
You have my thanks.

369
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:37,997
I'm not here to help you out.

370
00:29:38,080 --> 00:29:41,609
I'm here to take revenge on
Kaido, and that's the end of it.

371
00:29:41,840 --> 00:29:45,320
If you get in my way, I'll
crush you just like anyone else.

372
00:29:45,760 --> 00:29:47,466
Well, at least you warned me.

373
00:29:49,060 --> 00:29:49,890
Vroom!

374
00:29:52,880 --> 00:29:54,060
Go to hell!

375
00:29:56,200 --> 00:29:57,030
Amputation!

376
00:29:58,680 --> 00:29:59,720
And shadows.

377
00:30:11,380 --> 00:30:14,097
These pirates that Sir Kinamon
brought are really something.

378
00:30:14,180 --> 00:30:15,600
I think we can win this.

379
00:30:17,340 --> 00:30:19,000
Come on, you guys.

380
00:30:19,300 --> 00:30:20,300
What's the deal?

381
00:30:20,660 --> 00:30:23,077
The former warlord law
just showed up, too.

382
00:30:23,160 --> 00:30:24,737
We're getting overwhelmed out here.

383
00:30:24,820 --> 00:30:26,497
The enemy troops are teaming up.

384
00:30:26,580 --> 00:30:27,600
What do you say?

385
00:30:28,020 --> 00:30:28,900
Master Queen!

386
00:30:29,080 --> 00:30:30,577
You guys have more bad news?

387
00:30:30,660 --> 00:30:32,957
There's enemies at the
entrance to the island.

388
00:30:33,040 --> 00:30:35,857
Marco the Phoenix and Perospero
have joined forces and they...

389
00:30:35,940 --> 00:30:36,770
Ah!

390
00:30:37,600 --> 00:30:39,840
Watch out! Just say it!

391
00:30:40,460 --> 00:30:42,048
Don't leave me right there!

392
00:30:44,960 --> 00:30:46,240
Candy prison!

393
00:30:50,500 --> 00:30:52,320
You gotta be kidding me!

394
00:30:52,460 --> 00:30:54,989
Sure wasn't expecting
those two to team up!

395
00:31:00,300 --> 00:31:03,757
All right, it's time
to hunt some beasties.

396
00:31:03,840 --> 00:31:06,722
Look if they stick with
me and this will be easy.

397
00:31:07,140 --> 00:31:09,740
I'll make them all candy men soon enough.

398
00:31:09,980 --> 00:31:10,840
Wait and see.

399
00:31:15,680 --> 00:31:18,380
Alright you drunk
assholes, the party is off!

400
00:31:18,580 --> 00:31:21,060
Time to stop eating and kick some ass!

401
00:31:21,480 --> 00:31:23,440
Grab your weapons and go!

402
00:31:23,620 --> 00:31:25,860
We've got a raid on our hands!

403
00:31:33,840 --> 00:31:34,760
It begins!

404
00:31:39,920 --> 00:31:41,567
Kaido is out of the picture.

405
00:31:41,800 --> 00:31:44,918
But there are still three
lead performers down there.

406
00:31:45,840 --> 00:31:46,899
I must be patient.

407
00:31:47,600 --> 00:31:49,680
Please hold on, Lord Momonosuke.

408
00:31:49,940 --> 00:31:52,700
I promise I'll find a way to save you.

409
00:31:53,820 --> 00:31:54,650
Everyone!

410
00:31:55,380 --> 00:31:57,820
Let us reclaim the land of Wano!

411
00:32:24,700 --> 00:32:27,400
I heard what you said, Straw Hat.

412
00:32:27,760 --> 00:32:29,800
You're gonna kick my ass, huh?

413
00:32:31,040 --> 00:32:32,777
I accept your challenge.

414
00:32:32,860 --> 00:32:35,500
Let's see what you're made of.

415
00:32:42,660 --> 00:32:46,740
You're about to face the strongest
military power in the world.

416
00:33:15,820 --> 00:33:17,980
You have my face!

417
00:33:18,260 --> 00:33:19,320
Same to you.

418
00:33:19,600 --> 00:33:20,980
I'll catch up later.

419
00:33:49,160 --> 00:33:50,560
Damn that wind.

420
00:33:51,220 --> 00:33:52,457
Sobered me right up.

421
00:33:52,540 --> 00:33:54,137
A fight this epic!

422
00:33:54,220 --> 00:33:56,160
Should be out of the open.

423
00:33:57,260 --> 00:33:59,457
Reminds me of the last time we fought.

424
00:33:59,540 --> 00:34:02,400
How do you expect to win this fight?

425
00:34:02,860 --> 00:34:04,600
Now that Odin is dead.

426
00:34:04,980 --> 00:34:07,937
We don't have Odin, but there's
something else we do have.

427
00:34:08,020 --> 00:34:11,020
We were sure that Yugarra
would turn into a dragon,

428
00:34:11,200 --> 00:34:13,729
which means we would
have to fight outside.

429
00:34:21,060 --> 00:34:21,890
Huh?

430
00:34:22,280 --> 00:34:23,680
We have no fear.

431
00:34:24,200 --> 00:34:26,920
Red Heart anticipation
burns in our hearts.

432
00:34:27,120 --> 00:34:30,697
Our fury is about to be
unleashed on Yugarra.

433
00:34:30,780 --> 00:34:33,060
Ha, the meek tribe.

434
00:34:33,600 --> 00:34:34,620
Damn straight.

435
00:34:34,980 --> 00:34:38,098
They're the finest warriors
our kingdom has to offer.

436
00:34:43,820 --> 00:34:46,097
The snowfall is quite mild.

437
00:34:46,180 --> 00:34:50,020
The sky is clear and the full moon's out.
